[`provider_legacy.py:725`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:725).
The physics helper works in degrees; v2 converts the result to radians because
the inherited Q1 slot contract is radians. The implementation is at
[`q1_schema_v2.py:291`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-design-ws/q1_schema_v2.py:291).

[DERIVED] True off-axis is **not** recoverable from a serialized v1 row alone:
the row omits satellite/user/cell ECEF, and the sidelobed Bessel antenna gain is
not a one-to-one inverse for angle. It is recoverable at decision time because
both row builders still have the tape/provider identity and ECEF seams. The v2
resolver uses those exact seams and fails closed when they are absent; it does
not infer angle from gain or substitute elevation as a proxy
([`q1_schema_v2.py:335`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-design-ws/q1_schema_v2.py:335)).

