# PANELBUILD — Stage-C scoring-panel producer and receipt

## Outcome

The producer is [`scripts/build_stagec_scoring_panel.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/scripts/build_stagec_scoring_panel.py). It emitted:

- panel: [`artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.json`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.json), SHA-256 `92d5a80ff018c066ec95507da0f63bf4be5fa6802b3d15fafb8247b069dd53fb`;
- panel sidecar: [`artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.json.sha256`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.json.sha256);
- construction receipt: [`artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.receipt.json`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.receipt.json), SHA-256 `0ea296ee51aade5a19b44d0aa8c98d346ae405aa11004fd3c2cade2cf996ce83`.

The panel contains one common ordered catalogue per anchor. There is no arm-specific profile inventory: all five arms score the same `profiles` array, ordered with the base first and then by stable physical configuration ID before the IDs are SHA-256-shortened. Across the 20 anchors there are 19,780 profiles (963 minimum and 1,009 maximum per anchor), and no full-horizon profile was rejected as physically invalid.

Every profile carries C1 selected/reference states, C2 selected/reference states, the C3 coalition state, and its declared full-buffer physical outcome. Outcomes use all 48 realised boundaries and contain decoded bits, partial-payload DC joules, rate-target attainment/opportunities, service availability/opportunities, and handover events/opportunities. Handover events are counted from the declared prior-step incumbent using the engine's authoritative `beam_change`, `satellite_change`, and `cell_rekey` classifications. No demand cap is applied. Deadline numerator and denominator are both zero because the panel is not the online five-arm runner; consequently the scorer reports deadline-miss rate and per-arm timing/evaluation counts as unavailable instead of inventing them.

C1/C2 states come from the canonical, sidecar-authenticated exact-source view on 18 anchors. PANELCEIL's two nontrivial anchors require 147 action identities absent from those shortlist views (59 at global anchor 007 and 88 at global anchor 010); those rows were regenerated through the exact evaluator with the primitive fallback explicitly disabled. No provider-primitive feature state is present in the final panel.

The scorer's rigid v1 schema permits the reference object, information class, estimand, numerator, and energy boundary at panel identity/reference scope rather than alongside each scalar. The producer records them there, and the scorer copied them into every emitted result row. The exact numerator is:

> sum of saturated full-buffer successfully decoded forward-downlink information bits; rate target is a power-control setpoint; no demand cap

