## Fixture limitation — verified, not hidden

The nominated checkpoint is a synthetic smoke fixture. Its C1/C2/C3 input widths are 16/22/237 and its C3 member width is 38. The current production physical coalition encoder emits width 240: a fixed 234-value block plus six ordered global-resource features. For the fixture-only dry run, the producer emitted the first three of that ordered six-feature suffix, as required to reach width 237, and set top-level `synthetic_smoke_not_evidence` to `true`. This is a schema/integration test, not deployable C3 evidence.

The producer is checkpoint-width-aware. A future real width-240 Stage-C checkpoint will receive all six physical global-resource features and a separate checkpoint-keyed resume directory. It will not reuse the 237-wide fixture fragments.

The exact-source corpus currently has no authenticated `mcrl-v025-stagec-c3-coalition-shard-v2` view. Its own executed reader audit therefore fails closed before five-arm training. Consequently there is no real first-training checkpoint to score today. This panel closes the producer/schema/physics/reference gap and passes the required fixture dry run; it does not cure the separate missing-C3-training-corpus gap.

## Derived on paper

- The 20-anchor prefix composition is `6 complete steps × 3 carriers + 2 carriers at step 6 = 20`.
- The 19,780-profile total is the sum of the 20 emitted per-anchor catalogue sizes. This is inventory arithmetic, not an EE result.
- The 237 fixture width is `234 fixed encoder values + 3 ordered global-resource values`; production width 240 is `234 + 6`.

No score, loss, relative difference, or recovered fraction from the synthetic fixture is interpreted as physical or learned performance.

## Inferred

- The scorer's successful completion establishes schema compatibility and execution-path completeness for this fixture-shaped panel; it does not establish scientific validity of the fixture's learned scores.
- Because the selector-latency artifact uses different anchors and lacks complete per-profile outcomes, transferring its numbers would not have been a provenance-preserving reuse.
- A real first-training score remains contingent on generation of authenticated C3 training shards and a resulting real checkpoint. No modification to a sealed artifact can supply those missing joint labels; new authenticated physics/training output is required.

